# requirements-bpy.in : the Blender environment of plate3d.py (Blender as a Python module, GPL-3.0-or-later), a side
# Python 3.13 uv environment, because bpy 5.2.x declares requires-python ==3.13.*. This line is the one place the pin
# lives; plate3d.py runs the compiled lock and reads the version from it. After a change, compile the lock again from
# this folder:
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.13 requirements-bpy.in -o requirements-bpy.txt
# plate3d.py hashes requirements-bpy.txt into every plate's key, so a new lock makes each plate stale. uv run does not
# check the --hash lines of a --with-requirements file (uv 0.13.8, 2026-11-16): the exact pin of every package in the
# lock is what holds the set still. Version read from PyPI on 2026-11-16: 5.2.4 (2026-11-10) is the newest of the 5.2
# LTS line; 5.3.0 is a new minor and was not taken.
bpy==5.2.4
